{"name":"Slush","hex":"#d6cec4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"slush","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Half-melted snow or ice, generally located on the ground.","Liquid mud or mire."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To smear with slushy liquid or grease.","To slosh or splash; to move as, or through, a slushy or liquid substance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Slush","blocks":[{"text":"Slush, also called slush ice, is a slurry mixture of small ice crystals and liquid water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Slush_on_window_-_dusk.jpg/330px-Slush_on_window_-_dusk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slush","wikidata":"Q1047031"},{"title":"Slush (event)","blocks":[{"text":"Slush is a startup and tech event, held by Slush Oy company, annually in Helsinki, Finland. Slush facilitates meetings between the founders of startups and investors such as venture capitalists, accomplished with events such as matchmaking and pitching competitions. Slush aims to build a worldwide startup community. In 2021, Slush brought together 8,800 attendees from around the world to participate together in this global networking festival."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Slush_Black_Logo.png/330px-Slush_Black_Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slush_(event)","wikidata":"Q20921365"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Slush%5E_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1148909.jpg/500px-Slush%5E_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1148909.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Slush%5E_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1148909.jpg/500px-Slush%5E_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1148909.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped